  data:  # ba18
    kind: invariant  # ba18
    title: "INV-fusus follow-up: structurally-identical classes in different modules still share stable_id (18.94% post-fix residue, e.g. 49x TestAdaAnalysisUnavailable, 36x TestAnalysisRun)"  # ba18
    status: violated  # ba18
    priority: 3  # ba18
    parent:  # ba18
    tags:  # ba18
    - stable_id  # ba18
    - identity  # ba18
    - analysis_quality  # ba18
    - dogfood_round4_followup  # ba18
    isbefore: []  # ba18
    duplicate_of: []  # ba18
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ba18
    pr_ref:  # ba18
    description: "**Origin.** Follow-up to INV-fusus per [2026-05-19 dogfood validation comment](tracker://INV-fusus).\n\n**Symptom.** Post-INV-fusus (PR #3797, scheme v3) self-analysis on hypergumbo's own codebase:\n\n- 4282 Python class nodes, 0 missing `stable_id`, 3642 unique `stable_id`s.\n- 811 classes (18.94%) remain in collision groups.\n- Top collision examples: **49x** classes named `TestAdaAnalysisUnavailable` / `TestAsmAnalysisUnavailable` / `TestCapnpAnalysisUnavailable` (per-language fallback test classes with identical structure across modules); **36x** classes named `TestAnalysisRun` (literally same name, different test modules).\n\nINV-fusus closed the *same-module @dataclass collision* case (intra-module distinct-but-identical-body classes now disambiguate via folded body shape). The remaining 18.94% are a **different shape of collision**: structurally-identical classes in **different modules** still hash to the same `stable_id`.\n\n**Why this is a problem.** Two classes named `TestAnalysisRun` in `tests/test_cli.py` vs `tests/test_runtime.py` are semantically distinct symbols (different test cases for different subjects). They should not share a `stable_id`. Today they do, because the formula's `containing_stable_id` resolves to the module's `stable_id` — and either (a) the modules themselves collide, or (b) `containing_stable_id` is not actually folded into the ClassDef hash, or (c) some upstream step strips path information before the hash. Diagnosis spike required to determine which.\n\n**Invariant restated.** `Symbol.stable_id` must distinguish classes that live in distinct modules even when their body shape (method names, field names, base names) is identical — because module identity IS part of class identity in Python's import semantics.\n\n**Fix options.**\n\n1. **Verify the formula actually includes `containing_stable_id` for ClassDef.** If not (regression after WI-jagus), restore it. If yes, then the module's own `stable_id` must be colliding — escalate to INV-sotiv (file-kind / module-kind coverage gap) or open a new invariant for module-stable_id collision.\n2. **Fold a path-derived component into the class hash directly** (e.g., the parent package dotted name), as a guard against module-stable_id drift.\n3. **Document as accepted residue.** If consumers can always join on `(stable_id, canonical_name)` per the original INV-fusus option (3), then a residual 18.94% collision rate may be acceptable. This would need explicit documentation in the `Symbol.stable_id` docstring and ADR-0014.\n\nRecommended sequencing: scoping spike first to determine which root cause applies, THEN pick a fix. Don't pre-commit.\n\n**Verification target.** Post-fix, the 49x `TestAda…` / 36x `TestAnalysisRun` collisions should resolve to per-module-distinct `stable_id`s. Re-run self-analysis dogfood and assert collision rate drops to a smaller residue (target: ≤ 5%; any remaining residue should be semantically-distinct-but-empirically-indistinguishable cases requiring documentation rather than code fix).\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- `INV-fusus` (parent — closed; folded body shape into ClassDef hash; same-module case resolved)\n- `INV-sotiv` (sibling — stable_id missing for 7 kinds + 99.4% of files)\n- `WI-jagus` (closed — added `containing_module_stable_id` to the Python formula, scheme v2)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py:1526-1568` (`_compute_stable_id`)\n- ADR-0014 generalized symbol identity (phased rollout)\n- Notebook: 2026-05-19 dogfood validation transcript on INV-fusus."  # ba18
    fields:  # ba18
      statement: "Symbol.stable_id must distinguish classes that live in distinct modules even when their body shape (method names, field names, base names) is identical, because module identity IS part of class identity in Python's import semantics. Post-INV-fusus self-analysis shows 18.94% of Python class nodes (811/4282) still collide across modules — 49x TestAdaAnalysisUnavailable / TestAsmAnalysisUnavailable / TestCapnpAnalysisUnavailable per-language fallback classes, 36x TestAnalysisRun in different test modules."  # ba18
      root_cause: "Diagnosis spike pending. Three candidate root causes: (a) regression where the WI-jagus containing_module_stable_id input is no longer included in the ClassDef hash; (b) the module's own stable_id is colliding (escalate to INV-sotiv file/module kind coverage); (c) some upstream step strips path information before _compute_stable_id runs. Empirical signal is unambiguous (49x and 36x exact-name cross-module collisions), root cause is not."  # ba18
